# TaskLock

**TaskLock** is a backend task management API built with **FastAPI, PostgreSQL, SQLAlchemy, JWT authentication, Redis, Docker, and Pytest**.

The project is being developed as an industry-oriented backend system while progressively applying **system design, caching, authentication, testing, containerization, and scalability concepts**.

> **Current focus:** Backend engineering + System Design + DevOps fundamentals
> **Future direction:** CI/CD → AWS → GenAI/RAG → MLOps concepts

---

## Architecture

```text
                    Client
               (Postman / Frontend)
                       |
                       | HTTP / REST
                       v
                ┌──────────────┐
                │   FastAPI    │
                │              │
                │  Middleware  │
                │   Routers    │
                │ JWT Security │
                │   Pydantic   │
                └──────┬───────┘
                       |
              ┌────────┴────────┐
              |                 |
              v                 v
          ┌───────┐        ┌────────────┐
          │ Redis │        │ PostgreSQL │
          │ Cache │        │ Database   │
          └───────┘        └────────────┘
```

### Cache flow

```text
GET /tasks
     |
     v
   Redis
     |
   ┌─┴───────────┐
   |             |
 HIT           MISS
   |             |
   v             v
Response      PostgreSQL
                 |
                 v
            Store in Redis
                 |
                 v
              Response
```

### Write operations

```text
CREATE / UPDATE / DELETE
          |
          v
      PostgreSQL
          |
          v
   Cache Invalidation
          |
          v
      Redis cache
```

PostgreSQL acts as the **source of truth**, while Redis is used to improve read performance.

